+# Native horizontal system-area end prerequisite
+
+SystemManager.horizontalNeighbor scans the existing system encounter order backward for LEFT and forward for RIGHT, selecting the first strict y-overlap. SystemInfo.yOverlaps compares coordinate top/bottom (not Area bounds); touching edges do not overlap. SystemInfo.getRight returns left + width (without subtracting one); native GRID width is max staff right - min staff left + 1. Original computeSystemArea takes integer midpoints of the neighbor right and current left, or current right and neighbor left; absent neighbors use sheet endpoints. The native helper implements these rules directly and native GRID now calls it on coordinates produced from its staff curves. Existing single-column real inputs retain their outputs.
+
+The original probe calls unmodified horizontalNeighbor and computeSystemArea, including odd midpoints, skipping non-overlapping systems, encounter order, edge contact, positive horizontal neighbors and real observed Laura coordinates. Synthetic horizontal controls do not establish native raster layout discovery.
+
+Exact remaining dependency: system_graph::analyze rejects short staffs as multi_column_staff_neighbors. GRID currently constructs north/south areas from preceding/following systems rather than original StaffManager horizontal chains and SystemManager verticalNeighbors/getGlobalLine. Beam preparation also rejects clipped x ranges. Accordingly native_grid_ends returns unsupported_grid_horizontal_staff_chains when an actual horizontal neighbor is found, before exposing an incorrect area. No guessed sorting, nearest-x rule or fake successful multi-column pipeline is introduced. Next prerequisite is original staff horizontal-chain and vertical-neighbor construction upstream of global boundary paths. Full OMR remains unfinished and positive real-score rest conversion is not demonstrated. Full regression at this source remains unverified.
